      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T12:07:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Noting rather than objecting: this couples the shell to prose composed inside the dependency. _check() builds `f\"{context} not found{suffix}\"` (api/endpoints/readthedocs.py:233) and emit_error() prints `f\"Error: {message}\"` (typer_apps/rtd.py:46), with the context strings coming from project_details and project_version_details. I verified the match is exact at v0.8.2, including that Python\u0027s !r gives the single quotes you match on.\n\nIt is also fail-safe in the right direction -- a wording change in 0.8.3 makes the job fail loudly rather than silently concluding a project is missing and re-creating it -- and the \u003d\u003d0.8.2 pin in lf-env.sh contains the blast radius. So I am happy with it as merged.\n\nLonger term it would be worth asking lftools-uv for a distinct exit code for not-found, so shell callers do not have to match English. ReadTheDocs.project_exists() already exists in the library but is not exposed as a CLI subcommand, which is why string matching is currently the only option from a shell script.",
