      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T13:03:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch, fixed in patch set 5. One subtlety: with --from-branch, lftools-uv\u0027s not-found message names the slug (\"Version \u0027stable-scandium\u0027 of project ...\"), so the flag alone would have left a new branch with a slash unrecognised as missing. Patch set 5 passes the raw branch with --from-branch to project-version-details, project-build-trigger and project-version-update, so lftools-uv\u0027s version_slug() builds every request path. A shell copy of the rule (rtd_version_slug) names the version in the log and in the not-found match. I compared it with version_slug() from lftools-uv 0.8.2 over 14 branch names, including slashes, case, punctuation runs, edge hyphens and non-ASCII, and all matched. If the two ever diverge, the match fails and the job stops rather than treating the branch as missing. Tests added, as you suggested: Stable/Scandium discovers version stable-scandium, builds latest once, then the branch, then activates it; and a not-found naming the unslugified branch fails the job. Checked live against 0.8.2: all three commands accept --from-branch with --json and name \u0027stable-scandium\u0027. (Small correction for the record: --from-branch predates 0.8.2; it is in 0.7.6 too.)",
